    <div class="about-copy reveal">
      <p>
        I work at the intersection of advocacy and technology because I believe the systems we build determine who gets access to opportunity.
      </p>
      <p>
        At 7, I started advocating for education equity in California, first through Bithiah's Family Services and eventually by testifying before the California Senate and Assembly Education Committees on SB 897, the bill that made California's District of Choice program permanent, working alongside Senator Josh Newman and advocates from more than fifteen school districts statewide.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        "Tradition. Transformed. isn't a slogan. It's the method: take what advocacy already taught me, and build it into a system that reaches further."
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        At 18, I began building offline-first infrastructure in Uganda with Watoto, Intl., so students without reliable power or internet can build a resume. Most recently, as a Systems, Intelligence, and Monitoring Intern at the International Youth Alliance for Peace, I designed stakeholder intelligence systems that connected partner organizations across four countries in South Asia and Africa.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm currently pursuing a B.S. in Computer Science with a Minor in Data Science at Azusa Pacific University (expected December 2028), and working toward a Master's Degree in Machine Learning.
      </p>
    </div>

